self-improvement is not a destination  it's a journey  it needs practice and devotion  here are five hard to learn but really  important skills to improve your life  exponentially  one  being honest with yourself  the Journey of self-improvement starts  with being honest with yourself  it takes courage to tell yourself the  truth that you aren't perfect and you  must improve  most of the people would rather  mindlessly scroll social media or divert  their mind in meaningless things then  accept that their way of living is  lacking something and they must improve  so if you are not satisfied with your  life and want to improve your life start  by being honest with yourself  except you aren't perfect and  communicate with yourself know your  strength and weakness and put effort in  the things you want to improve  two  communication skill  communication is one of the most  important skill you can develop  the ability to say the things you want  to say the way you want to is priceless  proper communication skills will help  you in business networking dating and  many more  the most effective way to improve  communication skill is practicing  talking with people in every situation  possible  it will remove anxiety and fear attached  and train you to communicate effectively  three  time management  it sounds lame but time management is  one of the most underrated skill that  everyone should learn  managing time for work family and for  self is one of the hardest tasks in this  Modern Age  being busy doesn't mean being effective  with proper time management we can  complete our tasks in desired amount of  time and give time to ourselves and our  families  balancing work and play is important  nowadays people overwork or overplay and  the consequences follow  journaling and making routine are some  of the ways for Effective time  management  4.  consistency  in the world run by instant  gratification being consistent is the  key for improving life and long-term  success  self-improvement is not a destination  but a journey of consistently improving  yes you will fail at some point or you  will feel discouraged as you don't see  desired results but the one who keeps  working no matter what believing in  themselves and improving will eventually  get the desired results and success  the most effective way of being  consistent is to focus more on process  of improving than being perfect  five  being present in the moment  I can't stress this much but being  present in the moment is the most  hardest skill to learn yet most easiest  thing to do for us as human beings  being present in the moment is supposed  to be our default state but nowadays we  rarely are present in the moment as we  are constantly thinking about the past  that has already passed by the future  that is uncertain or holds infinite  possibilities  by thinking about past or future we are  depriving ourselves from all the  opportunity and beauty that life  provides us now  meditation is one of the most effective  way to train our mind to be present in  the moment  stop thinking about the past you can't  change or stop worrying about the future  that you can't know and just relax and  breed the soothing beauty of presence  and just live  you deserve this
 

